            "review_title": "Review at Dovado Pizza",
            "review_text": "ChewInRI\nEast Greenwich, Rhode Island1810 contributions\n0\nSuper weird pizza but plenty of good choices\nMar 2019 • Business\nI had a quick lunch with a colleague in Hanoi at Dovado pizza which was very near my hotel at the Landmark 72 building. The restaurant is located in a very pretty square that feels like a French street. The host spoke good english and the menu has English as well as pictures for those who aren't too sure what they are ordering. Service was a little slow, but the pizzas are made fresh so that is understandable. Besides pizza they offer pasta and meat dishes as well as salads and desserts.\nMy mushroom pizza sounded great on the menu but was super weird. It was drizzled with thousand island dressing (Why??) and the crust was stuffed with mashed sweet potatoes. I swear someone was drunk in the kitchen. \nI wouldn't say it was bad, it was just strange! Overall prices weren't cheap for Hanoi and this place caters to the local higher end business clientele. Good choice if you're in the area and need a change of pace for food or craving pizza.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten March 15, 2019",
