            "review_title": "Review at Dovado Pizza",
            "review_text": "Leean W\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam206 contributions\n0\nGem of a Find in Cau Giay\nFeb 2018 • Friends\nI generally only eat pizza at Pizza 4 P's as to me that's the ultimate delicious pizza but there is definitely a very tasty local pizza palour close to my workplace called Dovado. I often eat there if shopping in the Garden Centre close by, or have many deliveries if working late at work. My favourite is the Hawaiian Pizza - delicious with ample cheese, ham and pineapple and the garden salad with a refreshing dressing works well with it. The salad has a nice blend of mixed lettuce leaves, cherry tomatoes, grated carrots and olives although I do wish there were more tomatoes. However, I do find stingy amounts of tomatoes to be a strangely common feature in Vietnam, if included at all. Their 1000 Island dressing is generous and by far the most delicious ever tasted. Mention must also be made of their french fries - up there amongst the best in the city. They are crinkle cut which I usually don't enjoy, super crispy on the outside and soft and fluffy on the outside, a generous amount and always served piping hot. They are delightful. Finally the staff are lovely, very welcoming, caring and responsive. The place is quite basic looking, though clean and bright but altogether it is a wonderful place for a quick lunch when passing through the area and a genuinely tasty surprise.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 15, 2018",
